{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms","id":224006,"title":"3E: Any hints about Lunar shapechanging/warforms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-10T03:19:10-07:00","id":224006,"title":"3E: Any hints about Lunar shapechanging/warforms?","content":"I love lunars. Next to Alchemical's they're the most likely critter I play and if we're doing an Alchemical's campaign, I often say: hey, can I reskin a lunar as an Alchemical? Sadly, the mechanics do not always aid me in my love for the happy homicidal shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> So Has there been any hints, any comments from the developers before they pass out after a binge of drinking in how lunar shapechanging and warforms will be handled in 3E? Even the smallest spoiler? WE are legion. We demand it. We also have fleas, so we're a tad annoyed right now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T04:33:57-07:00","id":224035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms#post224006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Has there been any hints, any comments from the developers before they pass out after a binge of drinking in how lunar shapechanging and warforms will be handled in 3E? Even the smallest spoiler? WE are legion. We demand it. We also have fleas, so we're a tad annoyed right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are some things we know.<br /> For one, there'll be Charms that give you new ways to aquire a new form, beyond drinking a person's heartblood (an given example was sleeping with them).<br /> With the new combat system, different animals will have different moves and abilities that a human does not have. A tiger can gut a man with a claw-swipe. When a Lunar changes into the shape of an animal, they gain the abilities and moves of those animals.<br /> DBT will remain, but it will also be possible to make a Lunar who 'grows out' of that ability, and instead uses charms that only work when he is in his human form.<br /> Chimera-ism is less about being a Shoggoth this time around and instead about giving you interesting animal-hybrid-monsters as an option for your character.<br /> Shapeshifting in general is more about mythical shapeshifters and tricksters than about being the T-1000 or Mr. Fantastic.<br /> <br /> That's what I could find right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 08-10-2014, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T20:32:41-07:00","id":225614,"title":"","content":"I've heard about this ultra secret book called Barnacle &amp; Koi, which will feature an extensive list of marine and aquatic lifeforms as inspiration for lunar characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T20:37:26-07:00","id":225616,"title":"","content":"Lunars, in a minor editing mishap, were cut from the gameline entirely.<br /> <span style=\"color:white\">These are joke words. They are not serious.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T20:41:23-07:00","id":225619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=225616#post225616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars, in a minor editing mishap, were cut from the gameline entirely.<br /> <span style=\"color:white\">These are joke words. They are not serious.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is now a 4e Lunars speculation thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T20:41:29-07:00","id":225620,"title":"","content":"I saw Lunars wearing army pants and flip-flops, so I bought army pants and flip-flops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T20:51:37-07:00","id":225625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=225616#post225616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars, in a minor editing mishap, were cut from the gameline entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow an appropriate parallel given 1e/2e, where Lunars were a giant editing mishap played endlessly on repeat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T21:43:40-07:00","id":225640,"title":"","content":"Finally!<br /> <br /> I mean, I've never really gotten <i>why</i> you were even bothering with them for the new edition. They're just <i>baggage</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T22:15:06-07:00","id":225654,"title":"","content":"We've also been told that Lunars using DBT can't use Evocations. This, in turn, leads me to suspect that while there's probably not a whole lot required to invest for a baseline DBT--John's comments about outgrowing it suggest that it's fairly universal--it's probably the sort of thing you can ramp up into something truly nightmarish, so that not being able to use the evocations of your weapons isn't just blatant monstrous suicide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T22:20:30-07:00","id":225673,"title":"","content":"On that point, even if formlock stays around (*hacks, spits to ward off evil*) DBT has always been considered a &quot;true form,&quot; so despite your anima it's not like you can't start a fight in DBT to guarantee yourself a couple more persistantly-added Physical dice, and then shift back to your human form to fire up Evocations as circumstance or whim dictate.<br /> <br /> I just hope shifting is less...time-consuming at a baseline than it has been, by which I mean not requiring a ton of specialized shapeshifting-enhancing powers to be able to functionally play Beast Boy in combat without completely dumping your action economy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T22:23:46-07:00","id":225674,"title":"","content":"You guys joke, but I distinctly remember John mentioning that he had actually considered cutting Lunars from the line. While I am generally indifferent towards Lunars at best, I would have missed the Sun, Moon and Stars thing that the Celestials had going for them. Plus a player I game with regularly likes them a lot, so I would have been mildly upset on their behalf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T23:16:31-07:00","id":225694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=225654#post225654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've also been told that Lunars using DBT can't use Evocations. This, in turn, leads me to suspect that while there's probably not a whole lot required to invest for a baseline DBT--John's comments about outgrowing it suggest that it's fairly universal--it's probably the sort of thing you can ramp up into something truly nightmarish, so that not being able to use the evocations of your weapons isn't just blatant monstrous suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's not, &quot;evocations allowed in war form&quot; will be a common enough houserule, I'm sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T01:24:51-07:00","id":225749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=225694#post225694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's not, &quot;evocations allowed in war form&quot; will be a common enough houserule, I'm sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the choice was made probably because DBT is an Evocation on <i>you</i> that grows with native Lunar charms (figuratively and mechanically). Maybe Evocations will have to do with the &quot;human spirit&quot; and Lunars who have assumed their DBT are just enough of a step away from human that they can't invoke the Evocations.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling this will topic drift quite quickly. I'm sorry everyone <sup>I regret nothing!</sup>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T04:14:13-07:00","id":225814,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that if evocations get shut down in DBT, it'll be because DBT offers something that would be <i> devastating </i> with evocations, or offer something comparable to them power-wise. The devs aren't exactly the types of people to go &quot;let's screw over lunar fans AGAIN! This time with more forethought! Trolololololololol&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: or possibly slightly weaker than evocations, because of the &quot;outgrowing it&quot; angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T04:35:04-07:00","id":225821,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure no evocations in war form because there's a pretty big focus in DBT of becoming a living engine of destruction and power. Your direlance is just a pointy stick, the only advantage is that it's extra sharp and indestructible. The idea behind DBT is that even with a wooden spear a warform Lunar makes you wet yourself and cry.<br /> <br /> Kind of like those big action movies where the hero rubs out of ammo and then just proceeds to dismantle the enemy army one guy at a time with surprise neck snaps and thrown knives, ect. Then you realize that the LMG he had before was more of an accessory. The actual threat isn't the weapon, it's the guy behind it. Really he doesn't need it all that much, it's just convenient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T04:37:17-07:00","id":225824,"title":"","content":"I think DBT is, in a way, very much like your Evocations, except of coming from your weapon, it comes from you. So you can take it, get its first few abilities/charms, think that it'll be enough and try to become something else from there, or stick to it and become an absolute monster.<br /> I can totally see an Exalt who has a cool magic sword, relies on its great powers, but eventually decides that he needs to become a great swordsman instead of relying on the power of his weapon.<br /> <br /> Still, does that mean my Lunar can't be Sif the great grey wolf?<br /> <img src=\"http://darksouls.wdfiles.com/local--files/npcs/sif-the-great-grey-wolf-large.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T04:46:19-07:00","id":225828,"title":"","content":"No, that's fine. They only said Evocations crap out in War Form, so presumably Emperor Ox Expansion will still be fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T04:49:21-07:00","id":225832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=225824#post225824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, does that mean my Lunar can't be Sif the great grey wolf?</div> </div> </div> </div> From what I can tell, looking at a youtube clip of the fight, if we pretend Sif is a Lunar and that's her warform, it seems she's using Lunar Combat Charms, not Evocations. So, that shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> Remember that you can be a swordsman without learning a single evocation.<br /> (Just like how in 1E and 3E, you could be an unarmed fighter without learning a single Martial Arts Style)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/913-september","name":"september","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar913_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T04:49:59-07:00","id":225833,"title":"","content":"Besides, inability to use Evocations doesn't mean you can't just swing a giant magic sword while in beast form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T05:10:30-07:00","id":225842,"title":"","content":"And Lunars have Strength and Dex charms, so if the concern is that Lunars won't be able to hit hard and fast, that's not going to be a problem. At all. Because Lunars already do that without Evocations.<br /> It's more akin to shutting down Sorcery while in Warform (and I've never seen a DBT Sorcery build, so I don't think that would have been a problem anyway).<br /> <br /> And I kind of like that -- going DBT could be a little like Rage (without the compulsory kill-everything thing); there's you and your enemy, and everything else (weapons, sorcery, armor) is just in the way and inefficient compared to your own body.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Or, cinematically (because that's the direction Ex3 is trying to go), the focus in DBT goes on [<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>The Lunar killing things</i></span> with his giant sword], not on [the Lunar killing things <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>with his Giant Sword]</i></span>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 08-12-2014, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T05:42:17-07:00","id":225860,"title":"","content":"You could do a berserker- style &quot;trade sanity for power&quot; type thing, where there are a bunch of expansions turn you into a big honking rage monster before capping with a form that lets you keep the bonuses but only turns your hair blonde. And then there are two or three high-essence forms above that depending on your opinions of GT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T08:05:59-07:00","id":225978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=225814#post225814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that if evocations get shut down in DBT, it'll be because DBT offers something that would be <i> devastating </i> with evocations, or offer something comparable to them power-wise. The devs aren't exactly the types of people to go &quot;let's screw over lunar fans AGAIN! This time with more forethought! Trolololololololol&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'll cross-post some speculation of mine from another thread. I feel like there's a lot of potential for fighting styles dependent on a given Lunar's DBT, represented by a tree of Charms with DBT at its root, beyond more general Strength and Dexterity Charms (much as they'd also be applicable. This could also lend itself to another sort of &quot;giant spirit shape with sword&quot; tree of Charms for a style like Sif above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223888#post223888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, looking at DBT as another form, it stands to reason it, too, would have some minuses to go with its pluses. In EX3, one of those minuses is going to be a lack of Evocation access. It might also help to consider that it may be getting more than just a new minus. Personally, I have a hunch DBT is going to be even more powerful than it's been before. Aquillion had a very good point about one way that might be: in a land without common persistent dice-adders, the physical* Attribute-enhanced DBT-user is all the mightier. But it might extend beyond that. If Evocations are the big deal that they're meant to be and DBT is meant to be balanced against the lack of them, perhaps it could go even further than buffing up Attributes? I could see Charm trees building off of it,** developing powerful effects usable only while in DBT based off the unique synergy of human and beast it allows, much as Evocation arrays draw on the relationship of a wielder and her Artifact.<br /> <br /> From that perspective, a Lunar wouldn't be able to use Evocations while shifted into DBT, but would have access to something that might be seen as analogous, while still being able to shift back to human form if circumstances change and an Artifact's Evocations are needed. In this way, a Lunar swordsmaster with Evocations unlocked in a daiklave and great proficiency in DBT would be much like a Solar swordsmaster with Evocations unlocked in two daiklaves: neither can use both at once, but can gain clear benefits from being able to switch from one to the other as circumstances demand. It'd also be reasonable that such a hypothetical DBT-rooted Charm tree might be able to go places that Evocations wouldn't.<br /> <br /> * Sidebar: I wonder if it will still be restricted to Strength, Dexterity and Stamina next time. Perhaps it might be &quot;pick whichever 3 (or whatever) to boost and justify how;&quot; e.g. reaction time may quicken (Wits), as senses heighten (Perception) and the Lunar becomes all the more visually striking (Appearance). Even if the form is generally meant for combat, if there are numerous capabilities across the Lunar Charmset that would be great for battle and would benefit from heightened Attributes, I could see something like this working out. Eh, just musing.<br /> <br /> ** Fair warning: anyone who says something like, &quot;It's a Knack&quot; will make me laugh at them. We don't know if Knacks will even be a thing in EX3, much less if DBT will be among their number.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: or possibly slightly weaker than evocations, because of the &quot;outgrowing it&quot; angle. </div> </div> </div>I don't know. That's not really how I took the &quot;outgrowing it&quot; idea. I interpreted it more as not locking Lunars into going DBT as their one meaningful and obvious route of combat effectiveness, not that <i>all</i> Lunars gradually abandon DBT for Evocations. Besides, we already know Lunars aren't the greatest at Evocations (nor do we know exactly what that means), so options in or building off of DBT could very well be a match for those Evocations that they can access. They'd just presumably go to different places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T10:57:53-07:00","id":226109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foorish Shamurai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=225749#post225749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the choice was made probably because DBT is an Evocation on <i>you</i> that grows with native Lunar charms (figuratively and mechanically). Maybe Evocations will have to do with the &quot;human spirit&quot; and Lunars who have assumed their DBT are just enough of a step away from human that they can't invoke the Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does seem to be where they're going, but I'll just point out again that unless this changes, your DBT is considered your true shape. Meaning it's not a mix of you and something else. It is you. If you're killed, your body reverts to one of your true shapes because it is, truly, what you are. That's the whole point of the distinction between true and false shapes.<br /> <br /> So, if they want to say you can't use evocations while in your DBT or spirit shape, that's fine, I just hope they come up with some other rationale for saying it. Because &quot;it's not really you&quot; or &quot;you're not entirely yourself&quot; undermines the relationship between Lunars and their spirit shapes in a way I wouldn't like to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-12-2014, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:12:46-07:00","id":226115,"title":"","content":"What if it's <i>too much</i> yourself, and there's no more you left over to channel through your sword?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:18:03-07:00","id":226121,"title":"","content":"Honestly, that would work fine. Anything is preferable to &quot;your spirit shape is not compatible with your spirit&quot;, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:24:32-07:00","id":226127,"title":"","content":"It's not so much that it's not you, the devquote basically outright says it: it's you putting <i>all</i> of your energy into making yourself personally, physically, awesome, which leaves less energy for making you awesome in other ways (i.e. Evocations).<br /> <br /> I just hope DBT mechanics reflect this awesomeness better than they did before (a couple +1s and a few mutations is pretty underwhelming compared to the buildup the description creates)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:31:18-07:00","id":226133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226109#post226109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if they want to say you can't use evocations while in your DBT or spirit shape, that's fine, I just hope they come up with some other rationale for saying it. Because &quot;it's not really you&quot; or &quot;you're not entirely yourself&quot; undermines the relationship between Lunars and their spirit shapes in a way I wouldn't like to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>The old explanation re Evocations dealt with &quot;wearing power on the outside.&quot; I don't know why exactly this seems to have been abandoned because it made sense. Wearing your DBT, or a SMA Form Charm, or a Shintai, or...whatever Abyssals do externally (lol) is putting your own personal internal power on the outside.<br /> <br /> Solars don't have any native or close-to-native power that they wear externally, so it makes sense for them to be best at Evocations: they're not going to stack it with persistent enhancements from DBT or a Shintai. But for everyone else, you make a choice to either draw out from your weapon, or wear your power literally on the outside, and have to strike a balance what you can do at a given moment <i>even if you have both sets of power to choose from as the situation dictates</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:32:25-07:00","id":226136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226127#post226127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much that it's not you, the devquote basically outright says it: it's you putting <i>all</i> of your energy into making yourself personally, physically, awesome, which leaves less energy for making you awesome in other ways (i.e. Evocations).<br /> <br /> I just hope DBT mechanics reflect this awesomeness better than they did before (a couple +1s and a few mutations is pretty underwhelming compared to the buildup the description creates)</div> </div> </div> </div>Questions along this vein:<br /> 1. Can you use sorcery while in DBT in second edition?<br /> 2. Do you think you should be able to use sorcery while in DBT in third edition?<br /> <br /> I believe the answer to 1 is &quot;yes,&quot; but I'm not sure. I feel like the metagame would be made more interesting and complex if the answer to 2 were &quot;no.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:39:06-07:00","id":226144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226136#post226136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions along this vein:<br /> 1. Can you use sorcery while in DBT in second edition?<br /> 2. Do you think you should be able to use sorcery while in DBT in third edition?<br /> <br /> I believe the answer to 1 is &quot;yes,&quot; but I'm not sure. I feel like the metagame would be made more interesting and complex if the answer to 2 were &quot;no.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes, but sorcery wasn't that great for Lunars, because the tattoos shut down basically all sorcerous Shaping-type buff spells. Sorcery has <i>never</i> been good as a combat blast <i>especially</i> with other Exalted on the field (since you're standing there defenseless), its main benefit is utility and buff, and Lunars couldn't even buff themselves with it.<br /> 2. I think it should be possible, yes. <br /> <br /> Can you explain why you'd find that more interesting? For my position, I think Lunars need to stop getting shit on mechanically. Let them buff themselves with sorcery, or let a Lunar fly above the battlefield and unleash hell. We already know Shen, the sig Solar, uses his eagle Familiar to target spells on the battlefield. Why not let a Lunar fly up there and do it himself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:44:21-07:00","id":226160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226133#post226133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The old explanation re Evocations dealt with &quot;wearing power on the outside.&quot; I don't know why exactly this seems to have been abandoned because it made sense. Wearing your DBT, or a SMA Form Charm, or a Shintai, or...whatever Abyssals do externally (lol) is putting your own personal internal power on the outside.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think it's been abandoned? That's been among the few firm remarks from the EX3 team on the topic that I recall. If you've seen them say something else on the matter more recently, I'd be interested to read something newer.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This one. This is the only bit of conversation I've seen on the topic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's about how far your Essence can carry you, and where it goes. Lunars put all of their power into their Charms, and their Charms represent all of their creative, motive energy transitioning into a visible expression of power (like DBT). In essence, Lunars aren't as good at Evocations because their Charms already evoke most of their creative, transformative potential. This is also why they stop at Celestial Circle Sorcery and can't learn Sidereal Martial Arts. It is also why, when a Lunar goes DBT, his Evocations stop working. This also helps us balance Lunars who don't use DBT against Lunars who do.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Added dev quote because lol Gaius 08-12-2014, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:46:29-07:00","id":226165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226136#post226136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Questions along this vein:<br /> 1. Can you use sorcery while in DBT in second edition?<br /> 2. Do you think you should be able to use sorcery while in DBT in third edition?<br /> <br /> I believe the answer to 1 is &quot;yes,&quot; but I'm not sure. I feel like the metagame would be made more interesting and complex if the answer to 2 were &quot;no.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You can, though I've never seen anyone do it. I've never even seen anyone <i>want</i> to do it.<br /> I agree with you on 2","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:54:05-07:00","id":226170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226144#post226144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Yes, but sorcery wasn't that great for Lunars, because the tattoos shut down basically all sorcerous Shaping-type buff spells. Sorcery has <i>never</i> been good as a combat blast <i>especially</i> with other Exalted on the field (since you're standing there defenseless), its main benefit is utility and buff, and Lunars couldn't even buff themselves with it.<br /> 2. I think it should be possible, yes.<br /> <br /> Can you explain why you'd find that more interesting? For my position, I think Lunars need to stop getting shit on mechanically. Let them buff themselves with sorcery, or let a Lunar fly above the battlefield and unleash hell. We already know Shen, the sig Solar, uses his eagle Familiar to target spells on the battlefield. Why not let a Lunar fly up there and do it himself?</div> </div> </div> </div>(disclaimer: I love lunars, I really don't want them to be shat on either)<br /> <br /> Personally Id allow self-cast sorcery to shift non-dbt Lunars, but fail against DBT Lunars - somewhat along the line of &quot;Your true slef is overriding anything that would change your body, so much so that even your own sorcery can't do anything about it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mechanically it'd be mainly because Lunars can already get some pretty good buffs without needing Wood Dragon's Claw or Skin of Bronze or Imbue Amalgam. It could just as easily be part of their innate charmset (not <i>the same</i>, but similar enough).<br /> <br /> Also I don't even know if those spells will make an appearance in 3e.<br /> <br /> Also, you don't need to be in DBT to fly. You can just be a bird.<br /> Evocations get shut down specifically in War form, not in animal form. So that giant wolf with a sword can still use Evocations, and that eagle-lunar could (in this hypothetical scenario where DBT shuts down sorcery) still rain spells from the sky, just not while in DBT. Animal form =/= DBT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:57:09-07:00","id":226174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226160#post226160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes you think it's been abandoned? That's been among the few firm remarks from the EX3 team on the topic that I recall. If you've seen them say something else on the matter more recently, I'd be interested to read something newer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that logic had been abandoned or minimized after reading other quotes about Evocations on the wiki when John pretty much said &quot;Solars are the best at Evocations because Solars&quot; in a thread recently.<br /> <br /> I like that &quot;wearing power on the outside&quot; explanation a lot, mainly because it's sensical and doesn't imply that the system is playing favorites with splats, just expressing a new setting tenet in an understandable way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T12:00:07-07:00","id":226175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226165#post226165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can, though I've never seen anyone do it. I've never even seen anyone <i>want</i> to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does countermagic count?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226170#post226170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you don't need to be in DBT to fly. You can just be a bird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, for that matter you can just grow wings in human form too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226170#post226170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evocations get shut down specifically in War form, not in animal form. So that giant wolf with a sword can still use Evocations, and that eagle-lunar could (in this hypothetical scenario where DBT shuts down sorcery) still rain spells from the sky, just not while in DBT. Animal form =/= DBT.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, it strikes me as even more problematic to explain it by saying evocations are about &quot;human spirit&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T12:02:46-07:00","id":226178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226144#post226144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Yes, but sorcery wasn't that great for Lunars, because the tattoos shut down basically all sorcerous Shaping-type buff spells. Sorcery has <i>never</i> been good as a combat blast <i>especially</i> with other Exalted on the field (since you're standing there defenseless), its main benefit is utility and buff, and Lunars couldn't even buff themselves with it.<br /> 2. I think it should be possible, yes.<br /> <br /> Can you explain why you'd find that more interesting? For my position, I think Lunars need to stop getting shit on mechanically. Let them buff themselves with sorcery, or let a Lunar fly above the battlefield and unleash hell. We already know Shen, the sig Solar, uses his eagle Familiar to target spells on the battlefield. Why not let a Lunar fly up there and do it himself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, my position comes from an assumption that 3e sorcery will be useful in combat for more than buffing. If that's true, then DBT+Sorcery should be disallowed for the same reasons you would disallow DBT+Evocations - mostly, to avoid making DBT into some kind of &quot;super mode&quot; that stacks with everything and is therefore a cornerstone of all combat builds.<br /> <br /> Much as I like <a href=\"http://darksouls.wiki.fextralife.com/file/view/Chaos_Queen_Quelaag.png/477296330/480x339/Chaos_Queen_Quelaag.png\" target=\"_blank\">Quelaag</a> (pyromancy and an armored, chitinous hide covered in spikey bits makes for a pretty effective combo), I think it would be a bit of a loss if too many players felt compelled to play as her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T12:03:13-07:00","id":226179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226175#post226175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, for that matter you can just grow wings in human form too.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that stays around (I'm personally ambivalent on the subject especially with statements about being less The Thing/Alex Mercer and more mythic shape shifters like Loki - or to my mind, things Beast Boy might do).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226175#post226175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, it strikes me as even less sensible to explain it by saying evocations rely on &quot;human spirit&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression would be that the implication is even a sparrow spirit shape Lunar in the form of a tyrant lizard form might pale in power compared to that same Lunar in DBT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T12:06:41-07:00","id":226183,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I feel like sorcerous buffs are meant to be universally applicable (which was one of the big problems with Lunar tattoos that put them even further behind the curve). They've always stacked with old editions' &quot;external power&quot; like SMA Form Charms and Shintais, and if they stack with those there's no reason for them not to stack with DBT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T12:10:06-07:00","id":226186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226178#post226178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Admittedly, my position comes from an assumption that 3e sorcery will be useful in combat for more than buffing. If that's true, then DBT+Sorcery should be disallowed for the same reasons you would disallow DBT+Evocations - mostly, to avoid making DBT into some kind of &quot;super mode&quot; that stacks with everything and is therefore a cornerstone of all combat builds.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. So should Solars be barred from using sorcery while they're making use of their superior combat evocations? And should Sidereals be prevented while their martial arts or astrology or whatever is active?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-12-2014, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T12:23:37-07:00","id":226196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226186#post226186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. So should Solars be barred from using sorcery while they're making use of their superior combat evocations? And should Sidereals be prevented while their martial arts or astrology or whatever is active?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, but then Solars don't get the DBT option at all, and neither do Sidereals.<br /> <br /> My thinking is that when you separate out powers, it encourages people to either generalize widely (take a little each of evocations, DBT, sorcery, MA, etc. so you have more choices), or specialize deeply (focus exclusively on DBT OR MA OR Sorcery OR Whatever so you cannot be outcompeted in your chosen field). But when you make powers too easily synergistic, that almost forces people to become focused on multiple specialties in order to be competitive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T12:27:38-07:00","id":226200,"title":"","content":"&quot;Oh man, I can have Stamina Gift Charms, Soak Mutations AND Invulnerable Skin of Bronze? This is a no brainer.&quot; comes to mind. Which isn't the kind of thing I want at my table. &quot;Tactical Depth&quot; this is not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226186#post226186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. So should Solars be barred from using sorcery while they're making use of their superior combat evocations? And should Sidereals be prevented while their martial arts or astrology or whatever is active?</div> </div> </div> </div>Should every splat always have exactly the same bland mechanics for the sake of playing it safe in case people on the internet get upset that one splat works differently than an other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 08-12-2014, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T12:34:32-07:00","id":226206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226200#post226200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Oh man, I can have Stamina Gift Charms, Soak Mutations AND Invulnerable Skin of Bronze? This is a no brainer.&quot; comes to mind. Which isn't the kind of thing I want at my table. &quot;Tactical Depth&quot; this is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Oh man, I can have Sidereal Charms, astrological buffs, SMA Charms, AND Incomparable Body Arsenal? This is a no brainer&quot; comes to mind. And was feasible in past editions. Astrology may have not been good, but it was available.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh man, I can have Malfeas damage boost Charms, a Shintai, AND Invulnerable Skin of Bronze? This is a no brainer&quot; Etc. (Yes I know Infernals won't work the same, but there's no clue how they'll work, so whatever).<br /> <br /> Sorcery is historically designed to be synergistic with everything (and it was in 2e - except Lunar tattoos, because dumbness). Too much synergy to me would be DBT + full Evocations + Sorcery. But, again, assuming SMA Forms and Shintais and other &quot;external power&quot; are totally compatible with Sorcery and some use of Evocations, there's not much reason for DBT not to synergize with Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 08-12-2014, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T12:58:12-07:00","id":226256,"title":"","content":"Let's see if we can put this into a little bit better framework for purposes of analysis. There are several 'groupings' of powerful magic aside from standard charm use:<br /> <br /> 1) Personal transformation (DBT, Shintai, etc).<br /> 2) Sorcery/Thaumaturgy (different scales of things, but generally similar theme)<br /> 3) Evocations<br /> 4) Martial Arts<br /> <br /> Now lets see if we can define these a little bit more.<br /> <br /> 1) Personal transformation expounds on the theme of putting your personal growth and expressing your own Essence through yourself. You are the master of yourself, and push yourself so far beyond your own normal limits that you have nothing left for things that come outside of yourself. These things are part and parcel of your Exaltation, and no matter how hard you try, you will never be able to reach into someone else's style of mastery (Infernals never get DBT, Terrestrials never get Shintai).<br /> <br /> 2) Sorcery/Thaumaturgy is using the rules and shortcuts built into Creation, manipulated through Essence, to create effects. This is explicitly.a cross-Exaltation type of power. If you cast Death of Obsidian Butterflies, it is the same as someone else casting Death of Obsidian Butterflies. So long as you have the raw power to force your will across these procedures, you can do so.<br /> <br /> 3) Evocations are the mastery of tool use. Everyone can use tools, but some Exaltations resonate more strongly with tools than others. This also means pushing your essence outside of yourself and attuning yourself, changing yourself, to match your tools so that both you and your tool are the same. The tool becomes an extension of you.<br /> <br /> 4) Martial Arts represent an alternative form of Personal Transformation. Instead of using your essence and Exaltation to master your physical form, you use your physical form to master your working of Essence. You then use your mastery of essence to refine your physical form, and repeat the process. The more pure you are spiritually and physically, and the more in sync you are with yourself, the further you can go in Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> If everyone accepts these definitions (if not perfect, at least close enough for horseshoes and hand-grenades), we can then ask what should be compatible and what should not?<br /> <br /> 1 vs 2 <br /> 1 vs 3<br /> 1 vs 4<br /> 2 vs 3<br /> 2 vs 4<br /> 3 vs 4<br /> <br /> These six compose all possible combinations. We can go through these one by one and see what we get.<br /> <br /> 1 vs 2 (DBT vs Sorcery). My argument would be yes, these work together. The rules of Sorcery are part and parcel with the rules of Creation, and you are part of that. <br /> <br /> 1 vs 3 (DBT vs Evocations) I would say no. To push yourself this far, you must push your body to be in perfect attunement with your Essence. You cannot do this while also modifying your natural essence towards a tool that has its own essence structure.<br /> <br /> 1 vs 4 (DBT vs Martial Arts). These two are very close in theme. With MA, you use your body to master your essence. DBT, the opposite. In this case, I would suggest that while not incompatible, they are restricted. You cannot push your Essence into alien configuration through your natural body while pushing your body into alien configurations by using your natural essence. I would argue that someone in DBT can use those forms within their normal reach, but not above it. For example, a Celestial that can learn SMA cannot use them while in DBT. A terrestrial cannot manifest Celestial Martial Arts while using some variation of this power, like transforming into an elemental or something.<br /> <br /> 2 vs 3 (Sorcery vs Evocations). These two do not have any themes that would interfere with each other. In fact, certain evocations may even assist in Sorcery. Rather than being incompatible, I would put forward the idea that in some circumstances, these are synergistic, allowing a practitioner of both to reach a little further when using both than he could using only one or the other.<br /> <br /> 2 vs 4 (Sorcery vs Martial Arts). I don't know. I can see it several ways. I have no suggestions that are any better than others. My first thought is that, like DBT vs MA, you probably shouldn't be accessing any levels beyond your normal ability while doing so. A Terrestrial who has somehow initiated into Celestial Martial Arts and Celestial Circle Sorcery cannot use both at the same time, but can probably use Terrestrial Circle and Terrestrial Martial Arts at the same time.<br /> <br /> 3 vs 4 (Evocations vs Martial Arts). These do appear to have contradictory natures, but only if the Evocations are not in line with the particular MA. If you are using an MA that doesn't work with weapons, it doesn't work weapon Evocations. Same with MA and Armor. If you are using an MA that allows a daiklaive, then you can use its Evocations. If your evocation comes from a belt, and it isn't in line with your MA, then nope, can't use it. If it is, then sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T13:03:02-07:00","id":226260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226174#post226174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that &quot;wearing power on the outside&quot; explanation a lot, mainly because it's sensical and doesn't imply that the system is playing favorites with splats, just expressing a new setting tenet in an understandable way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, well, it <i>is</i> playing favorites. As with all design decisions, that idea that native Lunar Charms take up nearly all of their &quot;transformative power&quot; (which is a <i>bizarre concept</i> in and of itself - I mean, it's not like there'll be a point at which a Solar won't be able to learn more Lore Charms because they've used up all of their 'contemplative power') is a dev-level decision. You can't just sort of chalk it up to &quot;Oh this is how the setting works there's just no choice!&quot; Hell, even if that <i>was</i> some kind of core setting statement that you can only have so much &quot;transformative power&quot; it would be trivial to explain why Lunars can say &quot;fuck you&quot; to that rule in one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T13:04:26-07:00","id":226263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226196#post226196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not, but then Solars don't get the DBT option at all, and neither do Sidereals.<br /> <br /> My thinking is that when you separate out powers, it encourages people to either generalize widely (take a little each of evocations, DBT, sorcery, MA, etc. so you have more choices), or specialize deeply (focus exclusively on DBT OR MA OR Sorcery OR Whatever so you cannot be outcompeted in your chosen field). But when you make powers too easily synergistic, that almost forces people to become focused on multiple specialties in order to be competitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also a point that Sidereals, from what we've been told, won't have as high an access level to Evocations as the one that Lunars will apparently enjoy outside of their hybrid form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T13:20:43-07:00","id":226272,"title":"","content":"So solars get 3 apples.<br /> <br /> And Lunars get 4 apples.<br /> <br /> Their combined apple intake must be equivalent however (or the solars must have more, if you're so inclined)<br /> <br /> Should the Lunars get smaller apples, or only get to eat 3 out of the 4?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T13:20:59-07:00","id":226273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226200#post226200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should every splat always have exactly the same bland mechanics for the sake of playing it safe in case people on the internet get upset that one splat works differently than an other?</div> </div> </div> </div>I may just be someone on the internet to you, Fata-Ku, but I'm also someone who enjoys Exalted, I own every book from both editions and my opinion matters as much as yours does.<br /> <br /> And the issue is not that I'm upset because one &quot;splat&quot; works differently than others, so you can drop that BS. My issue is how it works and why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T13:43:35-07:00","id":226285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226273#post226273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may just be someone on the internet to you, Fata-Ku, but I'm also someone who enjoys Exalted, I own every book from both editions and my opinion matters as much as yours does.<br /> <br /> And the issue is not that I'm upset because one &amp;quot;splat&amp;quot; works differently than others, so you can drop that BS. My issue is how it works and why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then would you kindly contribute to finding a solution to said issue, instead of criticizing those who are by comparisons to other exalts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T13:44:12-07:00","id":226287,"title":"","content":"So I just want to check. DBT is Deadly Beastman Transformation right, I'm not thinking of the wrong charm/knack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T13:46:42-07:00","id":226290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226287#post226287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I just want to check. DBT is Deadly Beastman Transformation right, I'm not thinking of the wrong charm/knack?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You got it. I personally hate the acronyms that show up here all the time, but I fall into the trap too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T13:47:32-07:00","id":226291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226272#post226272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So solars get 3 apples.<br /> <br /> And Lunars get 4 apples.<br /> <br /> Their combined apple intake must be equivalent however (or the solars must have more, if you're so inclined)<br /> <br /> Should the Lunars get smaller apples, or only get to eat 3 out of the 4?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar apples are already bigger than Lunar apples. They have been historically and I think it's foolish not to believe that 3e Solar Charms are gonna be better than Lunar Charms in most cases. Solars have a whole circle of Sorcery access over Lunars. Solars might still be able to learn SMA with a tutor, where Lunars never have been able to. Yes, this is a lot of speculation (we don't know if Solars will have SMA access, for example). <br /> <br /> In the end Solar apples will probably be the equivalent of 5-6 apples, to the Lunars' 4. <br /> <br /> In any case, it's hard to compare Solar Evocation puissance with Lunar shapeshifting, figuring out how SCS compares to the best of Lunar shapeshifting, etc. I think the &quot;Solars have 3, Lunars have 4&quot; comparison is incredibly ineffectually simplistic because you're talking purely quantitative metrics versus qualitative. I imagine the intent is for a Solar and a Lunar to be able to give each other a good run for their money, all factors being equal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T13:47:40-07:00","id":226292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226287#post226287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I just want to check. DBT is Deadly Beastman Transformation right, I'm not thinking of the wrong charm/knack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. In 1e it was crazy powerful, in 2e it had mixed results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T13:53:32-07:00","id":226295,"title":"","content":"Evocations are a very broad class of power.<br /> <br /> If certain evocations stacked with transformation magic in a game breaking way, the general approach of the gameline would lead me to think that the approach would favor blocking combinations with those evocations, or even just imposing a hard stacking limit, not something crude like &quot;You can't use Level 3s, even when they're not broken&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> So it seems like that's the kind of tack they'd take, for the same kind of reasons they trust people to make sensible custom Charms rather than just blanket prevent customs. Of course, maybe it is just a circles thing, but that would just seem a little crude.<br /> <br /> There's no real sense in designing things to prevent tactically interesting combinations that aren't broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T14:10:47-07:00","id":226343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226285#post226285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then would you kindly contribute to finding a solution to said issue, instead of criticizing those who are by comparisons to other exalts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see what needs to be solved. You seem to think it's a problem if Lunars have access to sorcery in war form, so I think it's up to you to make the case what's wrong with it and provide solutions for how to fix it. I don't actually see any problem.<br /> <br /> I'm comfortable enough with 2E's arrangement - sorcery yes, transformation sorcery no (for tattooed Lunars). Losing access to spells like Invulnerable Skin of Bronze has never seemed such a big deal since Lunars can buff themselves up to literally unkillable levels just using their own innate powers, and for any other kind of transformation, their shapeshifting abilities provide ample solutions anyway. And permanent invulnerability to all hostile shaping effects is well worth the tradeoff IMO.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, Ejtaka's comment seems reasonable to me. I don't really have anything to criticize here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-12-2014, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T14:26:11-07:00","id":226352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226343#post226343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see what needs to be solved. You seem to think it's a problem if Lunars have access to sorcery in war form, so I think it's up to you to make the case what's wrong with it and provide solutions for how to fix it. I don't actually any problem..</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm... what?<br /> I was talking about why transformative sorcery doesn't affect lunars... which it already doesn't. There's nothing to propose or fix on my end...<br /> <br /> Unless you're referring to this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226165#post226165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you on 2</div> </div> </div> </div>Which isn't me engaging in any type of conversation about anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T14:31:33-07:00","id":226359,"title":"","content":"Well, you said the metagame would be more interesting if Lunars couldn't use sorcery in war form. Or you said you agreed with Semicasual that it would.<br /> <br /> I'm happy with it as it is, so there's nothing really for me to criticize about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T14:59:10-07:00","id":226418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226260#post226260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, well, it <i>is</i> playing favorites. As with all design decisions, that idea that native Lunar Charms take up nearly all of their &quot;transformative power&quot; (which is a <i>bizarre concept</i> in and of itself - I mean, it's not like there'll be a point at which a Solar won't be able to learn more Lore Charms because they've used up all of their 'contemplative power') is a dev-level decision. You can't just sort of chalk it up to &quot;Oh this is how the setting works there's just no choice!&quot; Hell, even if that <i>was</i> some kind of core setting statement that you can only have so much &quot;transformative power&quot; it would be trivial to explain why Lunars can say &quot;fuck you&quot; to that rule in one way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you get &quot;playing favourites&quot; out of &quot;making high-level design decisions based on aesthetics and motifs&quot;? Design decisions are going to affect different splats differently, but attributing that to simple favoritism seems crass.<br /> <br /> I tend to agree that DBT + Evocations is kind of a gross thematic clash. I would, for what it's worth, say the same thing about shintai + Evocations. The way Solar power manifests makes them less prone to this issue, but it also means that their native charmset tends to be less awesome, thematically, and forces them to go outside their splat for iconic &quot;flash&quot;. Solar charms and outside competencies are the strongest overall, but Solars are also the most strait-laced splat, and tend to suffer from being printed first. There's a lot going on here! Distilling it to &quot;playing favourites&quot; is a blunt rhetorical oversimplification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T15:03:09-07:00","id":226422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226291#post226291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solar apples are already bigger than Lunar apples. They have been historically and I think it's foolish not to believe that 3e Solar Charms are gonna be better than Lunar Charms in most cases. Solars have a whole circle of Sorcery access over Lunars. Solars might still be able to learn SMA with a tutor, where Lunars never have been able to. Yes, this is a lot of speculation (we don't know if Solars will have SMA access, for example).<br /> <br /> In the end Solar apples will probably be the equivalent of 5-6 apples, to the Lunars' 4.<br /> <br /> In any case, it's hard to compare Solar Evocation puissance with Lunar shapeshifting, figuring out how SCS compares to the best of Lunar shapeshifting, etc. I think the &quot;Solars have 3, Lunars have 4&quot; comparison is incredibly ineffectually simplistic because you're talking purely quantitative metrics versus qualitative. I imagine the intent is for a Solar and a Lunar to be able to give each other a good run for their money, all factors being equal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont't know. It's true for 2e and 2.5, but I'm kinda hoping Solars and Lunars are more on even footing in terms of charms in 3e -- in the sense that Solars are good overall and Lunars have peaks and valleys (and broadness) that puts them roughly on the same level (and from Dev Comments about power gaps I sorta hope that's what's going to happen). Then Evocations and DBT would roughly balance out, so that it doesn't matter, balance-wise, that you don't have one while you're in the other. Likewise with sorcery -- Lunars would get (advanced?) shapeshifting that puts Green Dragon's Claw, Skin of Bronze and Imbue Amalgam to shame (e.g. Claws of the Silver Moon, Stamina Charms/Gifts, DBT respectively), so it doesn't matter that you don't get them, because you already have things that are equivalent or better. It might be a little boring (which is why you mod the mechanics a bit) but it's be a not-too-bad way to compromise between people-want-things and flavor.<br /> <br /> edit: (spoilered for threadcrapping)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226359#post226359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you said the metagame would be more interesting if Lunars couldn't use sorcery in war form. Or you said you agreed with Semicasual that it would.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that translates into empty aggressive comments on your part? I'll keep that in mind.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 08-12-2014, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T15:26:55-07:00","id":226437,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I didn't like being told I was just &quot;upset that one splat works differently from another.&quot; I said that was a bullshit criticism because it was. If you want consideration, start by showing it.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T15:27:29-07:00","id":226438,"title":"","content":"One thing I was thinking about was that evocations seem to have a lot of transformative environment potential.<br /> <br /> So it would seem like evocations which change the environment could have an advantage for Lunars whose animal forms are adapted to that environment. Evoking wood to change the landscape into a thick forest / undergrowth might advantage a Lunar whose form would be adapted to that environment, evoking useful high winds for a flying Lunar, darkness for a nocturnal predator Lunar...?<br /> <br /> Or maybe that's beyond what evocations can do? Or is more appropriately an outgrowth of the transformation itself overflowing its container out into the environment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T15:36:37-07:00","id":226448,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226437#post226437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I didn't like being told I was just &quot;upset that one splat works differently from another.&quot; I said that was a bullshit criticism because it was. If you want consideration, start by showing it.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>You should take your own advice; this isn't considerate, useful or constructive; and was, in fact, a bullshit criticism:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226186#post226186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. So should Solars be barred from using sorcery while they're making use of their superior combat evocations? And should Sidereals be prevented while their martial arts or astrology or whatever is active?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are others, but they're quite possibly a misreading of your intent.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T15:43:03-07:00","id":226456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226422#post226422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont't know. It's true for 2e and 2.5, but I'm kinda hoping Solars and Lunars are more on even footing in terms of charms in 3e -- in the sense that Solars are good overall and Lunars have peaks and valleys (and broadness) that puts them roughly on the same level (and from Dev Comments about power gaps I sorta hope that's what's going to happen). Then Evocations and DBT would roughly balance out, so that it doesn't matter, balance-wise, that you don't have one while you're in the other. Likewise with sorcery -- Lunars would get (advanced?) shapeshifting that puts Green Dragon's Claw, Skin of Bronze and Imbue Amalgam to shame (e.g. Claws of the Silver Moon, Stamina Charms/Gifts, DBT respectively), so it doesn't matter that you don't get them, because you already have things that are equivalent or better. It might be a little boring (which is why you mod the mechanics a bit) but it's be a not-too-bad way to compromise between people-want-things and flavor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, dev statements seem to have been &quot;Solars on top, DBs at the bottom, other Celestials in the middle, with some effects that may surprise you, i.e. a DB Charm that is comparable to Solar stuff within a specific theme or motif.&quot; I like that, because 2e's strut, stratified power tiers got so boring so quick.<br /> <br /> It's just hard to say whether Evocations and DBT balance out. What about Solar Evocations vs Lunar Evocations (for non-DBT time)? That's what we can't gauge. Though we assuredly do know that Sorcery is supposed to be a lot better, that Solars will definitely have SCS and Lunars won't, and it's hard to argue that Solar Charmset + SCS + best at Evocations &gt; Lunar Charmset + DBT + other shapeshifting. At least generally speaking, since I expect Lunars to hit the Solar effect level on some stuff, as has been implied.<br /> <br /> It does matter though. Sorcery is universal; we haven't seen this to be different - if anything, it's becoming more true with the comments on mortal sorcerers. It's not helpful to &quot;put it to shame&quot; if a concept could be built around DBT and sorcery combinations, and I feel like the DBT/Evocation split is a lot more explainably thematic for Lunars than keeping the shitty &quot;can't buff yourself with spells because of these tattoos lol&quot; drek that we've gotten, that only serves to narrow what Lunars can do more and more.<br /> <br /> TL;DR the tattoos are shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 08-12-2014, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T15:44:49-07:00","id":226461,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/SHpZ69M.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T15:47:13-07:00","id":226465,"title":"","content":"That wasn't really even a criticism. I asked if the unique combat advantages of other types of Exalts should also not stack with sorcery, or if it should just be Lunars whose advantages don't stack with it. I mean you can probably tell I'm skeptical, but I haven't really taken a side in the argument except to say I'm happy with things as they are. I don't know how sorcery will work in the next edition so it's hard to say more than that.<br /> <br /> And is that the same cat in your profile pic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T18:05:20-07:00","id":226649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226290#post226290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You got it. I personally hate the acronyms that show up here all the time, but I fall into the trap too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok I was just making sure since I don't think I saw anyone refer to it by full name and I didn't play much with lunar characters, so it didn't come up. I'm gonna be honest I always thought it was just &quot;your warform gains a few extra attribute points as it becomes a more efficient ,&quot; so I'm not sure if I'm understanding the discussion on it with evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T18:18:23-07:00","id":226657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/224006-3e-any-hints-about-lunar-shapechanging-warforms?p=226649#post226649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok I was just making sure since I don't think I saw anyone refer to it by full name and I didn't play much with lunar characters, so it didn't come up. I'm gonna be honest I always thought it was just &quot;your warform gains a few extra attribute points as it becomes a more efficient ,&quot; so I'm not sure if I'm understanding the discussion on it with evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically, there was a developer comment that said Lunars in DBT don't get to use evocations. Most of the rest of the discussion was... well, its there, you can read it. The developer said it was unbalanced, and they had another theme in mind for them. DBT did more than just increase your stats, which it did very, very well. <br /> <br /> In total, it received:<br /> Extra stats, which were considered natural, so bigger excellencies.<br /> A bunch of mutations, which were extra powers, or extra dots, or stuff.<br /> <br /> You could also access Gift charms cheaper/faster, which were quite beneficial, and generally scene length buffs, like regeneration and Moonsilver claws. It also opened up an expansion that gave you more stat dots (Ogre Buff or something).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T18:29:58-07:00","id":226682,"title":"","content":"Gift charms being charms you can activate when you use DBT, to add extra effects. Like if you activated Halting the Scarlet Flow when you assumed your war form, you would regenerate a lethal health level of damage every action, even if unconscious, and could regrow lost limbs and organs, etc.<br /> <br /> The only problem with DBT in 2nd Edition was/is that it's so useful, it feels like every Lunar has to have it. I've never really wanted to play a Lunar without a war form, so that was never an issue for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T18:38:28-07:00","id":226686,"title":"","content":"It was great, and the only disadvantage was some essence outlay at the beginning transformation. And lack of subtlety in social situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:26:34-07:00","id":230555,"title":"","content":"I am slightly sad that I can't have KratoBear as my warform. Oh well, them's the breaks.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://fc07.deviantart.net/fs71/f/2012/164/b/b/bear_of_war___by_ilison-d53c97m.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}